1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,700
A player piano reads a perforated roll.
Here, each hole is a note you can edit.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,750
Punch C and E in the same column
to sound them together.

3
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:09,700
Set the tempo and press Play.
You are hearing the cabinet itself.

4
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:13,050
The moving column reads one sixteenth note at a time.
The instrument loops the bar.

5
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,400
Undo restores edits and tempo changes.
The roll stays on this device.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,450
Export a standard MIDI file for a sequencer,
or copy a link to the musical pattern.

7
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:22,120
Opening that link restores all sixteen columns
and the selected tempo.
